title: Soviet Election Campaign
card-image: img/cards/campaigning.svg?v=2
subtitle: Contest the factory and city soviets.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: campaigning_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; campaigning_timer = 3

Soviets are re-elected often. A campaign costs money for printing, halls and travel. [? if resources < 1 : We have nothing to spend. ?]

- @factories: Campaign in the factories. (1 resource)
- @garrisons: Campaign in the garrisons and at the front. (1 resource)
- @railways: Campaign among the railwaymen and postal workers. (1 resource)
- @joint: A joint list with our bloc partner. (1 resource)
- @villages: Campaign in the villages. (1 resource)
- @speeches: Send speakers out with no printed material.
- @easy_discard

@villages
view-if: player_party = 'sr' or player_party = 'lsr'
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no resources.
on-arrival: {!
RO.pay(Q, 1);
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: 7, soldiers: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 1, 0);
!}

Speakers went out to the volost assemblies and the village gatherings. The peasants listen to the party that calls itself their own.

@speeches
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 2, railway: 1});
!}

Without money for leaflets, the speakers went out on their own. It was not much of a campaign, but it was a campaign.

@factories
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no resources.
on-arrival: {!
RO.pay(Q, 1);
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 6});
RO.add(Q, {soviet_democracy: 1});
!}

Every shop floor that elects its deputies hears our speakers first.

@garrisons
choose-if: resources >= 1 and bol_regime = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 1 : We have no resources. ?][? if bol_regime = 1 : There is no garrison left that we may enter. ?]
on-arrival: {!
RO.pay(Q, 1);
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 6});
Q.militia = (Q.militia || 0) + 0.5;
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 1, 0);
!}

The soldiers' committees are less patient than the workers', but they still listen to the Soviet's own party.

@railways
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no resources.
on-arrival: {!
RO.pay(Q, 1);
RO.boost(Q, {railway: 7, workers: 1});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 2, 0);
!}

The railwaymen and the telegraph clerks have their own union and their own politics. They trust the party that listens to them.

@joint
view-if: ally_lvl >= 2 or ally_lsr >= 2
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no resources.
on-arrival: {!
RO.pay(Q, 1);
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 4, soldiers: 5, peasants: 3, railway: 3});
RO.add(Q, {rel_ally: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 1);
!}

A joint list showed one democracy instead of two parties. The Bolsheviks called it a deal between bureaucrats.
